From: mscharged-port
Subject: Carry GL resource markers at full width on LLP64
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; apply after 0646.

The game keeps GL resource markers in unsigned long variables and fields, and
0646 cast the remaining void* markers through unsigned long as well. That is
lossless for game memory, which the Windows build keeps below 2 GB, but native
markers are host records from the C++ heap and can lie above 4 GB. On 64-bit
Windows (LLP64) unsigned long is 32-bit, so such a marker was truncated and
ReleaseResource read a stray address: a goal replay crashed in
GLInventory::ReleaseLevel(-1) after DrawableNetMesh released its net pool.
Natively, the net mesh, loading and trophy casts use GLResourceMark and the FE
scene, FE model, impostor, front-end and movie markers are stored as
__UINTPTR_TYPE__. Nothing changes on LP64 or in the console spellings.

